From 1b51a95a089f59ad90e3469b33a74f02e1958d91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:51:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 59/60] wasm: the first code space must hold the far jump table
 without far jumps

d8-smoke's first wasm module (one function) died in
NativeModule::NativeModule -> AddCodeSpaceLocked ->
CreateEmptyJumpTableInRegionLocked(kFarJumpTable) ->
WasmCodeAllocator::AllocateForCodeInRegion:
"Check failed: kUnrestrictedRegion == region" - the region the module
was constructed with has no room for its far jump table.

13.6 gates the far-jump-table term of OverheadPerCodeSpace on
kNeedsFarJumpsBetweenCodeSpaces (12.4 counted it unconditionally):
without far jumps between code spaces the table is created only once
per module, in the first code space, so it is not a per-code-space
overhead.  But nothing else accounts for it, and AddCodeSpaceLocked
always creates it ("it contains the runtime stubs").  The initial
reservation is then ReservationSizeForWasmCode(halved estimate, n, 0)
= max(estimate + jump table, 2 * jump table), rounded up to the
allocation page.  For the smoke module that is a 4096-byte region
(estimate 275/2, jump table 32), and the far jump table is
BuiltinLookup::BuiltinCount() = 120 slots (103 builtins + 17 traps)
x kFarJumpTableSlotSize: 5280 bytes on ppc32 (11-word slots) - the
restricted allocation fails and the CHECK fires.  Upstream's 32-bit
targets survive on page slack alone (ia32 600, arm 960, riscv32 1920
bytes); on ppc64 the table is counted because far jumps are on.

Add the far jump table once to the initial estimate on targets without
far jumps between code spaces, next to the halving.  Growth
reservations (AllocateForCodeInRegion -> ReservationSizeForWasmCode
with total_reserved_so_far > 0) are untouched: FindJumpTablesForRegion
returns the first code space's tables for every later region on such
targets, so no later code space needs one.

This is the minimal, single-TU fix so the smoke battery can continue
on the installed build.  The configuration ppc32 actually wants is
ppc64's (its near jump slots are the same 26-bit relative branch), see
the following patch; under that configuration this branch is compiled
out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 v8/src/wasm/wasm-code-manager.cc | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/src/wasm/wasm-code-manager.cc b/v8/src/wasm/wasm-code-manager.cc
index 1fb5998..562b242 100644
--- a/v8/src/wasm/wasm-code-manager.cc
+++ b/v8/src/wasm/wasm-code-manager.cc
@@ -2481,6 +2481,13 @@ std::shared_ptr<NativeModule> WasmCodeManager::NewNativeModule(
                 (kSystemPointerSize == kInt64Size));
   if constexpr (!NativeModule::kNeedsFarJumpsBetweenCodeSpaces) {
     code_size_estimate /= 2;
+    // Without far jumps between code spaces the far jump table (one slot per
+    // runtime stub) is created once per module, in the first code space, and
+    // {OverheadPerCodeSpace} deliberately leaves it out; the initial
+    // reservation still has to hold it next to the jump table.
+    code_size_estimate += RoundUp<kCodeAlignment>(
+        JumpTableAssembler::SizeForNumberOfFarJumpSlots(
+            BuiltinLookup::BuiltinCount(), 0));
   }
 
   size_t code_vmem_size = ReservationSizeForWasmCode(
